  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.3.0-rc.1: Priority and per-partition fairness (new Priority and PartitionKey columns, new EnqueueAsync overload taking EmailEnqueueOptions); the failure reason is recorded on the row (new LastError and LastErrorOn columns); retry waits can be capped (MaxRetryBackoffSeconds) and can no longer overflow into an immediate-retry loop; optional outage pause (OutagePauseThreshold) so a mail server outage does not burn every queued email's retry budget; periodic wake (PollIntervalSeconds, default 120) so rows made due outside the process are picked up; the worker can no longer wedge after an exception or run two loops at once; a hung send is cancelled; stale claims count as a failed attempt; StaleClaimMinutes is bindable from configuration. SCHEMA CHANGE: the host must add four columns to the queue table, see the README section \"Upgrading to 2.3.0\".\n2.2.1: Fix stale-claim reclaim missing legacy rows — rows moved to Sending by pre-2.2.0 code have no NextAttemptOn deadline stamped and were orphaned forever; the reclaim now also recovers NULL-deadline Sending rows older than StaleClaimMinutes (by CreatedOn) back to Error for normal retry. No schema change.\n2.2.0: Atomic CAS claim of queued emails (ExecuteUpdateAsync Pending/Error -> Sending only if the row is still in the read status) so multiple worker instances can no longer double-send; stale-claim reclaim of rows left in Sending past a stamped deadline (reuses the existing NextAttemptOn column, no schema change); new RunHostedService option to gate the background worker on parked/standby instances while keeping EnqueueAsync available; configurable StaleClaimMinutes (default 10).",
